  "mach:judgement": "Assess",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The primary platform for individual patient data (IPD) sharing from clinical trials — 8,000+ trials, 5.2 million participants, 530+ resulting publications. Endorsed by NIH as an approved data sharing repository. Supported by 55+ members spanning major pharma (Pfizer, Roche, GSK, Novartis) and top academic institutions. Implements Five Safes Framework. Assess rather than Adopt for three reasons: access is entirely controlled (no open data tier), DUA is custom and non-negotiable (not a standard open licence), and there is no public API for programmatic discovery. Essential reference for any team requiring clinical trial IPD — assess whether your research plan meets the access criteria and institutional DUA requirements before submitting.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-02",
